  "summary": "Little foxes damage the flowering vines. The same animal name appears in scenes of ruined cities and scavenging, where jackal is also a plausible rendering. A different word describes a cupped hand measuring water or holding grain. Balaam’s donkey encounters a narrow passage with a wall on either side.",
