  "note": "Aramaic t and Arabic ṯ distinguish the fox word from the palm word, which has š in Aramaic. The passages give too little detail to identify the species in every setting. The place name Shaalbim preserves a b like Arabic ṯaʿlab, but no passage explains the town name. The relation of the narrow vineyard path to the cupped hand remains uncertain."
